course: dictionary
lesson: 3318
title: Small words, big meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are short but have more than one meaning. The letters alone do not tell you which meaning is right, so read the words around them. «She bought an EV to save money on petrol.» Here EV means a car that runs on electricity, because petrol is mentioned and the car is an alternative to it.
explain: Capital and small letters can change the meaning. EV is an electric vehicle, but eV is an electronvolt, a tiny unit of energy used in physics. Ask yourself what the topic is: a car on a road, or energy in a science lesson?
explain: When people type quickly, they shorten words. «Ev» may be a fragment of every or even. Check the sentence by trying the full word in its place. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: EV stands for electric vehicle: a car, bus or bike that runs on electricity from a battery.
fact: eV stands for electronvolt, a tiny unit of energy used in physics.
fact: An EV charger or EV charging point is where an electric vehicle gets power.
fact: In Turkish, «ev» means house, and its plural is «evler», as in the example sentence.
fact: Turkish plurals take -ler after e, i, ö or ü, and -lar after a, ı, o or u.
exercise: «She plugged her EV into the charging point overnight.» What does EV stand for? | Every vehicle | Easy venue | *Electric vehicle | Energy value
exercise: In a physics lesson, a student writes «eV». What does it stand for? | Electric van | Every value | Extra volume | *Electronvolt, a tiny unit of energy
exercise: In Turkish, «ev» ends in e. Which plural ending does it take? | *-ler | -ım | -lar | -evler
test: «The EVs in the car park were all charging.» What does EVs mean here? | Even vehicles | Energy values | *Electric vehicles, cars and buses that run on batteries | Every vehicles
test: «He typed ev, but he meant even, because he was typing fast.» In a quick text, ev is a short form of what? | Electric vehicle | *Every or even | Electronvolt | Evening
exam: A text says «Our family bought an EV and charged it at the EV charging point.» What does EV mean in this text? | *Electric vehicle that runs on electricity | Electronvolt, a unit of energy | Every or even | Evening
